WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:02.180
Tragedy in the Rain

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.150
Tokyo International Labor Show

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.730
That looks dangerous.
Can you see anything?

00:02:57.320 --> 00:02:58.690
There's a Type 7.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:02.160
Makes sense. It's probably
guarding the Labors.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.320
Why?

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:05.450
You need a Labor to
prevent Labor theft.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.160
Come on down.
We can go inside after lunch.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:13.790
What's the rush? We're on
duty for the entire show.

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:38.690
What's the big idea with
all these half-naked women?

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.610
A little glitter never hurts.

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:43.820
What if terrorists sent
in a bomb threat?

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:47.330
Then it's our headache.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.250
I think the girls are great!

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:51.080
Sucker!

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.920
They're just window-dressing!

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:07.220
The larger construction
Labors utilize linear motors...

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:10.390
but a look at the actuator reveals...

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:13.140
Sounds like they know
what they're talking about.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.520
I still don't like it.

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:19.820
That was good!

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.610
Ota and Shinshi are late.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:24.860
We're back.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:26.660
Izumi!

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:30.870
Answer quick: What's a linear actuator?

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:34.710
It's the drive unit for
the Ingram joints and limbs.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.170
What are its advantages?

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.000
Uh...

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:43.420
Back to the books!
Even the swimsuit models know that!

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:47.340
See anything interesting?

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:50.060
The economy model's on display.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.610
It's different from the picture.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:05.950
This is the prototype.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.120
Doesn't look too bad.

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.910
You can't tell anything
from the exterior.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:14.580
Hey, you!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:21.590
So this mass-produced model
is a match for the regular Ingram?

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:22.760
It's ugly!

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:27.130
How good is it, really?

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.010
I want concrete answers!

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:34.100
Can it handle a Type 7,
which is in the same weight class?

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:38.940
Yeah! If it can't do
that, we can't use it!

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:40.150
It's ugly!

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:50.950
So you two really
are an Ingram team?

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:52.790
I know we don't look like it.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.000
I'd like to see how
good you really are.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:58.710
Oh, just a bad joke!

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.460
Are you better at the game now?

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.550
I made it to Level 6!

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:07.130
That's all? You're no match for me!

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:12.140
I bet I can beat you in a real Labor.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.010
Bud!

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:16.600
Sorry, he doesn't know
what he's talking about.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.230
Kids say the darndest things.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.480
Hey, you two!

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:28.360
Wear your earplugs! What if there
was an emergency broadcast?

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:30.950
We'll see them again
soon enough. Let's go.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:35.740
You know them?

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.120
Sort of.

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:45.960
Don't go to the
convention too often.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:49.800
I have to memorize the layout.
Why can't we do it today?

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:50.840
Be patient.

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:54.510
But I want to take all the
Labors at the same time!

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:59.560
We don't want destruction;
we're after the Ingram movement data.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.560
There's no need to
disturb the general public.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.360
Our target audience will
definitely see the show.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.370
Labor Show Day 3

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.290
Final day discount!

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:25.710
Damn! The last day,
and no action!

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:26.670
Ota!

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.170
I guess we showed up for nothing.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:34.510
I wouldn't be too sure of that yet.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:39.600
There are an awful lot of
human-form Labors this year.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:45.560
It doesn't really help for
construction, but it sells well.

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.610
The future looks frightening.

00:07:49.570 --> 00:07:51.780
I'm more worried about the present.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:55.660
More divisions means
they need new Labors.

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:57.780
Don't you see?

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:02.500
Of course I do. But if they
want to swap out the Ingram...

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:05.750
they have to convince me
that their new machines are better.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:07.880
What proof do you need?

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:11.260
The best way is to watch it at work.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:17.100
You're right.
We need to see it in action.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:26.480
Asuma, even as a personal request...

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:31.530
Nothing big.
I just want to take it for a walk.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:35.490
Won't you get in trouble
for this? You're on duty.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.660
Don't worry about me.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:41.450
So? Is it just a lot of hype?

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.170
How can you say that?

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:48.340
Noa, I'm gonna do it!

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.090
I'm borrowing your movement disk.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.590
What are you doing?

00:08:57.220 --> 00:09:01.270
I'm going to check out
the economy model!

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.650
Don't put any bad data
on Alphonse's disk!

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.030
Do you understand the layout?

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.900
It looks a lot like an Ingram.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:19.620
Cheap monitor.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:23.950
I wish they'd made the cockpit airtight.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.470
Asuma, don't be too rough on it.

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:47.440
It's supposed to be
made for rough conditions.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.650
The ride's not too bad.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.900
Look what Shinohara's up to!

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.610
Giving a last-minute demo!

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:01.530
Well that wasn't our intention.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.340
Three months salary reduction!

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:21.600
Look at this! Shinohara is
using their mass-produced unit.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:24.560
We'll be able to test it, too.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.270
We'll begin soon.

00:10:29.810 --> 00:10:32.440
Roger. Bringing the Griffin
around to Point A.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.740
Bud, you're up.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:17.360
What? Shinohara decided to
test out the economy model?

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:20.570
It's unauthorized!
He's deserting his post!

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:23.870
The Captain may let him
get away with this, but I won't!

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:26.540
I won't let him get away with it.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:31.420
Of course not! But Shinohara
isn't taking his duties seriously!

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:35.460
Is three months
salary reduction enough?

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:39.300
We'll have to talk about it.

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:43.340
He <i>did</i> leave his post,

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.470
but we need to test
the economy model.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:52.600
It's a bonus for the force.

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:53.600
Softy!

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:59.570
But isn't this really bad
for Division 2's reputation?

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:01.780
It's not that bad.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:06.320
Don't worry, Yamazaki!
I'll save our reputation!

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:10.000
I'll put a halt to Shinohara's
selfishness... whatever it takes!

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:11.870
Whatever it takes?

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:20.800
Just watch!
I'll put a halt to this!

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:25.390
How is that going to
make things better?

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:26.640
Do something.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:27.850
I'll get the command car.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.810
And there it is!

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.020
The players are all on stage.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:40.820
Hey, Ota! What's up?

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:45.320
Listen, Shinohara!

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.410
Leave that machine immediately,

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.910
or I'm going to have to pull you out!

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.710
Is that officer one of yours?

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:54.580
Yes.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:59.840
Oh, drat! If I'd only kept quiet,
you wouldn't have known.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:02.840
Captain, aren't you
going to stop this?

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:05.340
I order you to exit!

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:11.970
You can't reason with Ota
until you've pinned him to the mat.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:15.270
You want a piece of me?

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:19.610
Are you threatening me?

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.150
Nanny-nanny boo-boo!

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:26.110
He does a pretty good
nanny-nanny boo-boo.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:29.570
Do you know who you're talking to?

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.620
Yeah, that's why I dare you!

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:37.000
You'll pay for that!

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:38.830
They're really going to fight!

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.920
Salary reduction: Six months.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:52.890
What the hell are you doing?

00:13:54.640 --> 00:14:00.020
Sorry, I was in a hurry.
I have to set up for the next exhibition.

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:03.480
The next show doesn't
set up until tomorrow!

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.320
What's this?

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:12.870
Gas! Everyone get back!

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:18.620
The next show starts right now!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:20.040
Why, you!

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:21.790
Be careful!

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:23.750
Now, Bud.

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:44.440
What is this?

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:02.580
Call Division 1 for backup. Hurry!

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:07.840
Izumi, mobilize machine 1. Hurry!

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:08.800
Roger.

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:16.970
Asuma's using my movement disk!

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:19.680
Hold it right there.

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:22.650
Stop now, or you'll have to face me!

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:28.990
Shinohara, that's no ordinary Labor!
Pull back, you amateur!

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:32.610
Amateur?
I had the same training you did!

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:37.330
Here I come!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:57.350
Hold on! Hold on! Hold on!

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:05.440
What? The whole lower half
of this Labor is shaking!

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:19.950
He's fast!

00:16:27.790 --> 00:16:29.500
This looks bad.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:33.760
Did you see that?
It moves like a living thing!

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:39.890
Hiromi, get me as close
as possible in the command car!

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.180
Wait, Izumi. What are you planning?

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:46.650
I have to save Asuma and
get my movement disk back!

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:49.900
You'll be crushed.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:52.940
But without it, machine 1 can't move!

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.490
Wait for Division 1 to get here.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:59.620
Besides, how are you going
to rescue Asuma from that?

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:06.500
Mr. Utsumi, this one
isn't much of a challenge.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:10.000
I'm not impressed with
Shinohara's latest offering.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:15.970
Bud, forget that piece of junk.
We want the Ingram's disk.

00:17:19.680 --> 00:17:22.140
You'll regret this!

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.440
Ota, you idiot!

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:34.400
You... you... you... idiot!

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.860
I told you to stay out of my way!

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:47.620
I'm going!

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.250
Take that!

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.300
Bud, stop playing and finish him off.

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:06.230
Asuma!

00:18:13.570 --> 00:18:15.030
Here's your disk.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:20.570
It's not as bad as it looks.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:24.200
This Labor couldn't keep up
with your programmed movements.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.750
But machine 1 can do it.

00:18:54.570 --> 00:18:57.940
Mr. Utsumi, I've defeated the Ingram.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:04.740
Then hurry and open the hatch.

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:06.040
Chief, the smoke!

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.250
We've come this far.
Another minute won't matter.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.260
Damn you!

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:30.520
You can still move?

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:34.860
Don't worry, Izumi.
Asuma's injuries aren't serious.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:38.110
But Ota's in trouble.
Help him out.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:43.990
Division 1 sure is late.

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.960
You're under arrest for
reckless endangerment,

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:03.340
destruction of property
and assault! Freeze!

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:07.680
There was another Ingram?

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:10.390
Chief, the rain has
destroyed our smoke screen.

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:14.100
Sorry, Bud. Time to withdraw.

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:17.610
At least we've gained some
valuable data for the Griffin.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.990
This area is dangerous.
Please evacuate.

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.280
Richard Wong!

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.920
You fool! Why did you shoot?

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:39.800
Sorry, Sir. She got too close.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:42.420
And she recognized you from
your days in Hong Kong.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:49.390
Bud, things just went wrong
in a big way. Withdraw immediately.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:55.140
If you won't come at me,
then I'll come at you.

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:08.830
What?

00:21:42.900 --> 00:21:44.490
I could have beaten you!

00:22:26.320 --> 00:22:27.610
It's a nightmare...

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:48.220
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:51.930
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:54.260 --> 00:22:58.180
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:07.690
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:10.610
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:15.200
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:17.870 --> 00:23:19.870
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:22.710
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:22.960 --> 00:23:26.880
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:33.390
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:38.640
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:41.190
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:41.190 --> 00:23:44.400
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:44.650 --> 00:23:48.480
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:50.860 --> 00:23:54.660
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:56.830 --> 00:24:00.710
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:07.340
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:12.010
This story is fiction...

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:12.010
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:23.600
Division 2 is cut to less than half!
<i>Then</i> we get notice that the Griffon...

00:24:23.850 --> 00:24:25.440
just crashed into the
mountains near Chiba.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:28.320
There are shadows of Utsumi
behind this mess, I can just feel it.

00:24:28.320 --> 00:24:30.280
To keep this corruption from
coming to the surface,

00:24:30.280 --> 00:24:33.860
Shaft Security Systems is being
brought in to clean up the mess.

00:24:33.860 --> 00:24:36.530
Now a mysterious stranger from
abroad appears to take on Shaft!

00:24:37.120 --> 00:24:40.500
Next episode: Reunion.
Target Locked On!

00:24:39.740 --> 00:24:45.250
Next episode

00:24:39.740 --> 00:24:45.250
Reunion
